+## Declaring Runtime Requirements
+
+If your integration depends on a specific runtime, declare that in `runtimeCapability` so Ecopages can fail during config finalization instead of during startup.
+
+```typescript
+class CustomIntegration extends IntegrationPlugin {
+	renderer = CustomRenderer;
+
+	constructor() {
+		super({
+			name: 'custom-integration',
+			extensions: ['.custom'],
+			runtimeCapability: {
+				tags: ['node-compatible'],
+				minRuntimeVersion: '20.0.0',
+			},
+		});
+	}
+}
+```
+
+Available tags:
+
+1. `node-compatible`
+2. `requires-node-builtins`
+3. `bun-only`
+4. `requires-native-bun-api`
+
+Use the smallest declaration that matches reality. For example, an integration that only needs standard Node-compatible APIs should not declare Bun-only requirements.
+
